# GENEALOGIX Repository Code Owners
#
# GitHub auto-requests every listed owner of a changed path as a reviewer on
# each PR. Whether a code-owner approval is ALSO required to merge depends on
# the org-internal "Main Protection" ruleset's require_code_owner_review
# setting, which is not represented in this repo and can change independently.
# (SECURITY-POSTURE.md maintainer-verifies the ruleset's existence and general
# posture, but NOT this flag; this specific flag's value and the decision to
# enable it are tracked in #258.) This file deliberately does not assert the
# flag's current value, to avoid the stale-state drift trap. CODEOWNERS is
# last-match-wins and a matched owner set REPLACES earlier matches; the
# catch-all stays FIRST and any narrower rule must list EVERY owner it wants,
# not just the extra one.
#
# Learn more: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Both maintainers are code owners of every path, so GitHub auto-requests both
# as reviewers on each PR (minus the PR author, who cannot review their own) --
# deliberate cross-review / bus-factor insurance for a 2-person team. This
# covers the whole tree: go-glx/, glx/, specification/, docs/, website/,
# .github/, the tooling dirs, and root manifests. Do NOT add per-directory
# rules that just re-list these two owners (no-ops + drift).
* @noahbjohnson @isaacschepp

